15 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Box plots showing expression levels of LRRN family genes \(LRRN1, LRRN2, LRRN3, LRRN4, LRRN4CL\) across various TCGA tumor types. The left column displays expression in tumors, while the right includes both tumor and normal samples, with red and blue colors indicating cancer and normal tissue, respectively. Data are presented as Log2\(FPKM+1\).) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Box plots show the expression levels of LRRN1, LRRN2, LRRN3, LRRN4, and LRRN4CL genes in relation to tissue type, AJCC stage, tumor size, lymph node involvement, and metastasis in breast cancer. Each subplot displays differences in expression between categories with associated p-values indicating statistical significance. Expression levels are presented in log scale on the y-axis.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Kaplan-Meier survival curves for molecular subtypes of breast cancer, labeled A to E, depicting the expression levels of LRRN1 to LRRN4CL. Subtypes include All, Luminal A, Luminal B, Her2+, and TNBC. Each graph compares high and low expression groups over time, with hazard ratios and log-rank p-values indicated. The number at risk is detailed below each curve, showing patient distribution over time.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (A series of biological experiment results featuring multiple graphs and images analyzing LRRN1 overexpression effects. Panels A and B show bar graphs of LRRN1 expression in MDA-MB-231 and MCF-7 cells, respectively. Panels C and D display optical density measurements over five days. Panels E and F illustrate colony formation assays. Panel G presents migration and invasion assays, with results in panel H. Panel I features cell migration images at intervals, analyzed in panel J through a line graph of wound healing. Western blot analyses in panels K and M show FAK, MMP2, MMP9, and GAPDH levels, with quantification in panels L and N. Statistical significance is shown throughout.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Image with a grid of multiple panels displaying various analyses and data visualizations related to gene expression and signaling pathways. Panels A to D present bar charts and diagrams of module and signaling pathway analyses. Panel E shows a Venn diagram illustrating overlapping pathways. Panels F to R display scatter plots examining correlations between gene expressions. Panel S includes a bar graph comparing gene expression levels in different cell lines. Panels T and U show survival probability curves in relation to gene expression levels over time. Statistical values and annotations are labeled throughout the panels.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (A multi-panel scientific figure includes several charts and graphs. Panel A presents a ranked interaction analysis with various pathways. Panel B displays the correlation between PD-L1 expression and the PD-1 checkpoint pathway. Panels C to O show scatter plots of different immune cells and markers correlated with LRRN1, annotated with R and p-values. Panel E presents violin plots comparing ESTIMATE, Immune, and Stromal scores between two groups. Panel F contains a heatmap of immune cell group expressions. Panel G is a bar chart of different immune cell types across two groups. Panels P to S show box plots comparing drug sensitivity between groups L and H, with significant p-values.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
